  "verbalization": "Tranilast, a drug primarily used for its anti-inflammatory properties, is linked to Asthma through a series of molecular pathways involving allergic and vasomotor rhinitis. The evidence suggests that Tranilast may modulate inflammatory responses by targeting pathways that lead to the development of Asthma. Specifically, Tranilast is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis and Allergic Rhinitis, both of which are inflammatory conditions that can progress to Asthma. The involvement of Flunisolide and Fluticasone Furoate, which are corticosteroids, further supports a role in reducing inflammation, potentially contributing to the development of Asthma. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that Tranilast may exert a beneficial effect on inflammatory processes that underlie Asthma. However, the exact mechanism by which Tranilast influences Asthma remains to be fully elucidated, and further research is needed to confirm its therapeutic potential in this context.",
